<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="open-pilgrimages" version="1.1"><metadata><name>Kohechi (Mountain Route)</name><desc>The mountain route between the two sacred centres of the Kii Peninsula: 63 km from Koyasan to Kumano Hongu Taisha, crossing three passes above 1,000 m. Four days, with the nights at the river-valley settlements of Omata, Miura-guchi and Totsukawa Onsen. The high point is Obako-dake at 1,344 m, and the route carries about 3,500 m of ascent against 4,280 m of descent.</desc><copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"><license>https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/</license></copyright><link href="https://open.pilgrimag.es/kumano-kodo-kohechi"><text>Kohechi (Mountain Route)</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Kohechi (Mountain Route)</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="34.212827" lon="135.587402"/><trkpt lat="34.212626" lon="135.587342"/><trkpt lat="34.212532" lon="135.587263"/><trkpt lat="34.212467" lon="135.587207"/><trkpt lat="34.206945" lon="135.587078"/><trkpt lat="34.206976" lon="135.586965"/><trkpt lat="34.207040" lon="135.586736"/><trkpt lat="34.207109" lon="135.586543"/><trkpt lat="34.207184" lon="135.586362"/><trkpt lat="34.207270" lon="135.586219"/><trkpt lat="34.207379" lon="135.586073"/><trkpt lat="34.207407" lon="135.585999"/><trkpt lat="34.207397" lon="135.585650"/><trkpt lat="34.207442" lon="135.585570"/><trkpt lat="34.207512" lon="135.585545"/><trkpt lat="34.207566" lon="135.585555"/><trkpt lat="34.207926" lon="135.585865"/><trkpt lat="34.207972" lon="135.585887"/><trkpt lat="34.208002" lon="135.585895"/><trkpt lat="34.208034" lon="135.585879"/><trkpt lat="34.208171" lon="135.585804"/><trkpt lat="34.208212" lon="135.585797"/><trkpt lat="34.208255" lon="135.585807"/><trkpt lat="34.208455" lon="135.585938"/><trkpt lat="34.208496" lon="135.585951"/><trkpt lat="34.208539" lon="135.585946"/><trkpt lat="34.208575" lon="135.585907"/><trkpt lat="34.208697" lon="135.585621"/><trkpt lat="34.208765" lon="135.585506"/><trkpt 